Pope Francis is back at the Vatican this  morning after the Catholic World Youth  Day rally in Panama Seth Doane traveled  with the Pope as he discussed the  church's upcoming summit on sexual abuse  and his fears of a bloodbath in  Venezuela  Seth is with us from now from Rome good  morning good morning Pope Francis told  us onboard that plane that he believed  that expectations should be deflated for  that much-anticipated February summit  here at the Vatican that will be looking  into the issue of clerical sex abuse he  said that sex abuse is not just an issue  in the church but it is a problem  through all of humanity he said the  first step is to recognize the issue and  in some cases bishops don't know what to  do he spoke out strongly against  abortion and offered some personal  advice he had four mothers who had had  one he said that they should sing  lullabies to their children in heaven he  spoke out in favor of celibacy for  priests and sex education in schools and  he also made news regarding the conflict  in Venezuela while he did not take sides  he said he stood with the suffering and  was terrified of a bloodbath  John sat down in Rome thanks so much  Seth
 

